CHAPTER OBJECTIVES
After completing this chapter, students will be able to
• define terms and acronyms associated with industrial hygiene;
• identify the classes of occupational hazards;
• describe basic toxic effects and routes of entry;
• identify various agencies and organizations providing support to industrial
hygiene;
• characterize the roles and responsibilities of the industrial hygienist (IH);
• identify the various disciplines that form the foundations of industrial
hygiene;
• understand the primary approaches to protecting workers in their work
environment;
• describe the primary controls employed by IHs to control workplace
exposures;
• explain the various types of sampling that may be conducted by the IH;
• understand the concepts of equipment calibration and accurate laboratory
analysis;
• identify how industrial hygiene fits into an overall occupational safety and
health program;
• analyze how IHs respond to emerging hazards; and
• plan how IHs can prepare for pandemics and public health emergencies.
